# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Both values are public-by-design browser
# credentials — they ship in the built bundle. Security comes from the
# Authorized JavaScript origins (client ID) and the HTTP referrer + API
# restrictions (API key), not from keeping these hidden.

# OAuth 2.0 Client ID — APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth 2.0 Client IDs
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# API key, restricted to the Google Picker API
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Local development also needs, in the Google Cloud Console:
#   - OAuth client > Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173
#   - API key > Website restrictions:               http://localhost:5173/*
#   - APIs enabled: Google Drive API, Google Picker API
#   - Consent screen in Testing mode: your own account listed under Test users
# A missing localhost referrer on the API key surfaces as the Picker reporting
# "The API developer key is invalid", not as a referrer error.
